      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Herein we report the clinical presentation and radiographic findings of a patient with a known history of multiple nonossifying fibromas, also known as the Jaffe-Campanacci syndrome, who presented with persistent pleuritic chest pain after a fall and was found to have a small pulmonary embolus. The presentation, pathophysiology and management of the syndrome are briefly discussed."},
